Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Governance: add Standards-conformance BDR scope-boundary
 addendum

Appends a non-normative clarifying addendum to
docs/specs/19-governance-bdr-policy-framework.md, recording that a
Business Decision Record is triggered by the substantive strategic/
business question being answered, not by a change crossing module or
application boundaries. Corrections that only bring existing
implementation into compliance with an already-approved Standard
(DESIGN_SYSTEM.md) or Architecture Principle (02-core-product-
principles.md Section 2.11) introduce no new capability, business
philosophy, operational policy, or business-domain decision, and do
not require a BDR or Policy document on that basis alone. Such
corrections proceed through the applicable Standards/Architecture and
engineering-governance path (Rule 8 Assessment, Implementation
Authorization) directly.

Distinguishes this from the existing cross-cutting BDR namespace
(BDR-0004/0008/0009/0012), whose members are cross-cutting because
their strategic subject matter lacks a single module home -- a
different reason than this addendum's boundary, which turns on
whether a strategic question is being answered at all.

Cites the UI Readability Amendment (docs/engineering/ui-readability-
amendment.md, closed out and committed at c71bfa0) as the precedent
this addendum records.

Pure append: 0 deletions, 68 insertions, one file. Sections 1-4 and
the document's original Governance Notes/Lifecycle content are
unmodified. Does not touch platform-engineering-governance-standard.md,
CLAUDE.md, the UI Readability Amendment or any of its governance
artifacts, or any source file. Does not alter or reopen commit c71bfa0.

Approved by: SABUSHIMIKE Masceni, Product Architect. 2026-08-20.
